  "title": "UC San Diego Resting State EEG Data from Patients with Parkinson's Disease",
  "description": "Resting-state EEG recorded at UC San Diego from patients with Parkinson's disease and healthy controls. Patients were recorded in two sessions, on and off dopaminergic medication, while controls completed a single session. The dataset includes participant demographics and UPDRS and MMSE clinical measures, and is curated in BIDS format for studying oscillatory and waveform characteristics of Parkinson's disease.",
  "methods_description": "Resting-state EEG was recorded with a BioSemi system and stored as .bdf files. Healthy controls had one session and Parkinson's patients had two, one on and one off dopaminergic medication. UPDRS ratings were collected by trained laboratory personnel rather than a board-certified neurologist.",
